# `poll process` is not optional: it's the only thing that acts on the
# registry's passwdReminder, so a scheduler that silently stops running it
# ends with an expired EPP credential and every call failing. This file is
# the sidecar's whole job -- see compose.yaml's scheduler service.
#
# EPPITNIC_CONFIG_DIR/EPPITNIC_VAR_DIR are set as image ENV (see the
# Dockerfile) and would normally just be inherited, but cron implementations
# differ in what environment they hand a job -- vixie-style cron resets it to
# a fixed minimal set, and only variables declared in the crontab itself
# survive that. BusyBox crond's actual behaviour here isn't verified (no
# Docker on this machine to check), so they're declared explicitly below
# rather than assumed inherited. Do not "tidy up" this duplication with the
# Dockerfile's ENV -- without it, `poll process` looks for
# /app/config/config.php, finds nothing, and fails every five minutes: a
# scheduler that's silently broken on an otherwise healthy stack.
EPPITNIC_CONFIG_DIR=/data/config
EPPITNIC_VAR_DIR=/data/var

# su-exec, not root: config.php and the selftest notes this writes have to
# be owned the same as the web tier that also reads and writes them (see
# docker/entrypoint.sh's chown). /proc/1/fd/1 is this container's own PID 1
# (crond itself, run in the foreground -- see compose.yaml) -- the usual way
# to make a cron job's output land in `docker logs` instead of nowhere.
*/5 * * * * su-exec www-data /usr/local/bin/eppitnic poll process >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1

# Shipped unconditionally: `session keepalive` prints nothing and exits 0
# whenever the `keepalive` setting is off (the default), so this needs no
# image change when an installation turns it on. Once a minute, refreshing
# comfortably inside nic.it's 300s idle timeout -- see docs/INSTALL.md's
# "Session keep-alive".
* * * * * su-exec www-data /usr/local/bin/eppitnic session keepalive >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1

# Shipped unconditionally: `domain sync` prints nothing and exits 0 whenever
# the `domain_sync` setting's `enabled` flag is off (the default), so this
# needs no image change when an installation turns it on. Every 5 minutes,
# alongside `poll process` -- see docs/INSTALL.md's "Domain reconciliation".
*/5 * * * * su-exec www-data /usr/local/bin/eppitnic domain sync >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
